return await tools.hold_arm({
  first: { plan: "plan-a", phase: "A1" },
  second: { plan: "plan-b", phase: "B2" },
  leading: "plan-b",
  reason: "Both plans rewrite `HitRecord` in `src/hittable.rs` and `Sphere::hit` in `src/sphere.rs`. plan-b (B1, already committed) adds `front_face`/`u`/`v`, keeps `#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]`, and makes `HitRecord::new` the only construction; plan-a A1 adds `material: Rc<dyn Material>`, drops `Copy`, and builds the record via a struct literal in `Sphere::hit`, so its signature, derive list, `point`-attribute line and construction contract all contradict plan-b's, and `src/main.rs:ray_colour` plus its sphere tests change under both. Each branch passes alone, but merging needs a design choice on how the material joins a `HitRecord::new`-built record without a second constructor or a `Copy` record."
});

